      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It might seem like a small thing to you, but alcohol can significantly alter the way Ambien works in your body. One glass might not cause a huge reaction for everyone, but it can increase the risk of excessive drowsiness, dizziness, impaired judgment, or even overlap in their effects that lead to unintentional overdose situations. Yes, some people might not experience any issues with a small amount, but it's risky and not advised without professional guidance. It could be worth considering other relaxation techniques or delaying your alcohol intake until after you've slept well with Ambien, rather than combining them immediately.",
      "source": "target",
